From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Maria Blasco <josep.maria.blasco@epbcn.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:29:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: command environments (ADDRESS) written in JavaScript

.JSCommandHandler (wasm/web/js.cls) makes a JavaScript function, of any
realm, one of the interpreter's command handlers (RFE #882, trunk
r13288): .CommandHandler~register(name, .JSCommandHandler~new(fn)),
~deregister(name), stacked, with handlers, handler and the core's errors
(a name with no handler, an empty name).  Its COMMAND calls fn(command,
ctx) on the Rexx thread that issued the command: what fn returns is RC
(undefined or null: 0; a Promise, or any thenable, is waited for); ctx is
the command's .CommandContext as a RexxProxy, every message forwarded
with the core's name (getVar, setVar, hasVar, dropVar, variables, [],
input, output, error, raise, raiseError, raiseFailure, environment,
pending, finish, isRedirected, isValid), the tests answering booleans;
in the page its calls give Promises.  A JavaScript exception is SYNTAX
98.900 where the command was issued (ADDITIONAL as for any JavaScript
exception); a condition of Rexx that the function lets through is raised
there as itself, and so is any other condition that Rexx code the
function calls raises (USER: COMMAND is a native method, js_command in
web-js.cpp, so no Rexx activation stands in between); a HALT that such
code leaves untrapped is a HALT there.  .JSCommandHandler~new(.nil), or of anything but a
function, is SYNTAX 93.900.
- From the page (ooRexx.js): a session's addCommandEnvironment(name, fn)
  and removeCommandEnvironment(name) (.JSSession: register and
  deregister, answering what they answer), and
  start({commandEnvironments: {NAME: fn}}), which stops the session if one
  fails.
- Tests: wasm/tests/js-commands.rex (62 checks, Node and the worker's
  realm; in qualify-node-cli.sh and web-api.py), web-api.py "js commands
  page" (a function of the page) and "session commands".
Not part of the posted RFE.
